00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:29.840
I put down the glass, move next to her to wash it.
这座桥似乎并没有给她留下什么深刻印象。

00:24:30.560 --> 00:24:35.920
She's exactly my height and smells of liquid detergent and has tiny beautiful moles on her neck.
这是最短的路。

00:24:36.780 --> 00:24:41.340
Here, she says, putting out her hand, but I finish it and go back to the den.
我去年刚来时他也是这么说的。

00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:44.460
Do you know what she wants us to do, I say to Wayne?
我想看看乡下的风景。

00:24:51.620 --> 00:24:54.460
Wayne is sinking the bolts into the slate with the Makita.
反正雨太大，什么也看不见。

00:24:54.900 --> 00:24:56.440
You can't do it, he says.
我很想问她是否爱她的老板，但我转而问她，你觉得美国怎么样？

00:24:57.280 --> 00:24:57.560
Why not?
她转头看着窗外的巨型广告牌。

00:24:58.340 --> 00:25:00.060
Kid, we have to finish this.
这一切我都不觉得奇怪，她说。

00:25:00.880 --> 00:25:02.100
I'll be back before you know it.
当我们驶过桥面时，我把手放进她的膝盖上。

00:25:02.140 --> 00:25:03.740
A quick trip, in, out.
我把它留在那儿，手心朝上，手指微微蜷曲。

00:25:04.380 --> 00:25:06.120
Kid, he stands up slowly.
有时候你就是得去尝试一下，哪怕明知行不通。

00:25:06.920 --> 00:25:08.220
He's nearly twice as old as me.
她缓缓转过头，望向桥缆之外、曼哈顿和哈德逊河。

00:25:09.480 --> 00:25:10.860
I go to the window and look out.
华盛顿高地的一切都是多米尼加风格的。

00:25:12.080 --> 00:25:14.480
New ginkgos stand in rows beside the driveway.
你走不了个把街区就会路过一家基斯奎亚面包店、一家基斯奎亚超市或一家基斯奎亚酒店。

00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:19.340
A thousand years ago, when I was still in college, I learned something about them.
如果我把卡车停下走出去，没有人会把我当成送货员。

00:25:19.340 --> 00:25:48.720
living fossils unchanged since their inception millions of years ago you tagged Charlene didn't you sure did he answers I take the truck keys out of the toolbox I'll be right back I promise we reached the Washington Bridge without saying a word is this the best way she asks asks.
我可以是那个在街角卖多米尼加国旗的人。

00:25:48.960 --> 00:25:50.920
The bridge doesn't seem to impress her.
我可以是在回家找我姑娘的路上。

00:25:51.680 --> 00:25:52.860
It's the shortest way.
当我们到达她住的那条街时，我向一个穿着宽松垮裤的小孩打听那栋楼，他用小指指了指台阶。

00:25:53.940 --> 00:25:55.660
That's what he said when I arrived last year.
去年我到这儿时，他就是这么说的。

00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:57.250
I wanted to see the countryside.
我想去看看乡村。

00:25:58.120 --> 00:25:59.900
There was too much rain to see anything anyway.
反正雨下得太大，什么也看不清。

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:06.060
I want to ask her if she loves her boss, but I ask her instead, how do you like the States?
我想问她是不是爱她的老板，但转而问她，你觉得美国怎么样？

00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:09.280
She swings her head across the billboards.
她把头一晃，掠过那些广告牌。

00:26:10.120 --> 00:26:11.960
I'm not surprised by any of it, she says.
她说道，这一切我都不觉得意外。

00:26:12.920 --> 00:26:16.020
As we cross over the bridge, I drop my hand into her lap.
当我们开过桥时，我把手放进她的膝头。

00:26:16.900 --> 00:26:19.600
I leave it there, palm up, fingers slightly curled.
我把它放在那儿，手心朝上，手指微曲。

00:26:20.540 --> 00:26:23.580
Sometimes you just have to try, even if you know it won't work.
有时候你就是得去尝试，哪怕明知不会成功。

00:26:24.540 --> 00:26:29.760
She turns her head slowly, facing out beyond the bridge cables, out to Manhattan and the Hudson.
她缓缓转过头，望向桥索之外、曼哈顿和哈德逊河的方向。

00:26:35.980 --> 00:26:37.860
Everything in Washington Heights is Dominican.
华盛顿高地的所有东西都是多米尼加风格的。

00:26:38.760 --> 00:26:45.240
You can't go a block without passing a Quisqueya bakery or a Quisqueya supermercado or a Hotel Quisqueya.
走不了街区，你就会路过基斯克亚面包店、基斯克亚超市或是基斯克亚酒店。

00:26:45.830 --> 00:26:49.880
If I were to park the truck and get get out, nobody would take me for a delivery man.
如果我把卡车停下并走出去，没人会把我当成送货员。

00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:53.200
I could be the guy who's on the corner selling Dominican flags.
我完全可以成为在街角卖多米尼加国旗的那个人。

00:26:54.140 --> 00:26:55.820
I could be on my way home to my girl.
我也可以是正走在回女友家路上的人。

00:26:57.060 --> 00:27:02.740
When we reach her block, I ask a kid with a sag for the building, and he points out the stoop with his pinky.
当我们到达她所在的街区时，我向一个穿着宽松裤子的男孩打听那栋楼，他用小指指了指门廊前的台阶。

00:27:03.100 --> 00:27:09.660
She gets out of the truck and straightens the front of her sweatshirt before following the line that the kid's finger has cut across the street.
她下了卡车，整理了一下卫衣的前襟，然后顺着那小孩手指划过街道的方向追去。

00:27:10.940 --> 00:27:11.940
Cuídate, I say.
“保重，”我说。

00:27:19.900 --> 00:27:45.920
wayne works on the boss and a week later i'm back on probation painting the warehouse wayne brings me meatball sandwiches from out on the road skinny things with a seam of cheese gumming the bread was it worth it he asks me he's watching me close i tell him it wasn't did you at least get some hell yeah i say are you sure why would i lie about something like that Homegirl was an animal.
韦恩去找老板求情，一周后我又回到了缓刑期，在仓库里刷漆。韦恩从路上给我带肉丸三明治，那种细长的面包，里面夹着一层像口香糖一样粘牙的奶酪。“这值得吗？”他问我，他紧紧盯着我。我告诉他一点也不值得。“你至少捞到点什么了吧？”“见鬼，当然啦，”我说。“你确定吗？”“我怎么会拿这种事撒谎呢？那妞简直是个野兽。”

00:27:46.120 --> 00:27:47.600
I still have the teeth marks.
我身上现在还有牙印呢。

00:27:48.560 --> 00:27:49.560
Damn, he says.
“真行啊，”他说。

00:27:57.740 --> 00:27:59.440
We're back on the road a week later.
一周后我们又上了路。

00:28:00.820 --> 00:28:04.280
Buckinghams, Imperials, gold crowns, and dozens of card tables.
白金汉牌、帝国牌、金冠牌纸牌，还有几十张纸牌桌。

00:28:05.260 --> 00:28:09.640
I keep a copy of Pruitt's paperwork, and when the curiosity finally gets to me, I call.
我留了一份普鲁特的单据复印件，当好奇心终于战胜我时，我拨通了电话。

00:28:10.880 --> 00:28:12.420
The first time I get the machine, machine.
第一次我听到的是录音机，录音机。

00:28:13.060 --> 00:28:24.740
The next two times I'm in the Bedminster area, Pruitt picks up and says yes, but on the fourth time she answers, and the sink is running on her side of the phone, and she shuts it off when I don't say anything.
接下来两次我在贝德明斯特地区时，普鲁特接了电话并说“在”，但第四次她接电话时，电话那头正开着水龙头，而当我一言不发时，她把水龙头关掉了。

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:27.700
Was she there, Wayne asks in the truck.
“她在那儿吗？”韦恩在卡车里问。

00:28:28.520 --> 00:28:29.300
Of course she was.
“她当然在那儿。”

00:28:30.440 --> 00:28:35.020
He hands me the map, and my fingers trace our deliveries, stitching city to city.
他把地图递给我，我的手指追踪着我们的送货路线，将一座座城市串联起来。

00:28:35.940 --> 00:28:37.360
Looks like we've gotten on everything, I say.
“看来我们把所有地方都跑遍了，”我说。

00:28:38.220 --> 00:28:40.040
Finally, he yawns.
最后，他打了个哈欠。

00:28:40.600 --> 00:28:41.260
What's first tomorrow?
“明天第一站去哪儿？”

00:28:42.600 --> 00:28:47.760
We won't really know until morning when I've gotten the paperwork in order, but I take guesses anyway.
直到早晨我把单据整理好之前，我们其实都不知道，但我还是瞎猜起来。

00:28:48.640 --> 00:28:49.260
One of our games.
这是我们的游戏之一。

00:28:49.780 --> 00:28:53.020
It passes the time, gives us something to look forward to.
这能打发时间，让我们有所期待。

00:28:53.540 --> 00:28:56.300
I close my eyes and put my hand down on the map.
我闭上眼睛，把手按在地图上。

00:28:56.900 --> 00:28:59.700
So many towns, so many cities to choose from.
有那么多的城镇，有那么多的城市可供选择。

00:29:00.740 --> 00:30:04.240
