00:33:15.940 --> 00:33:17.020
That's the charm of Empire City.
这就是帝国城的魅力所在。

00:33:17.500 --> 00:33:21.280
You hold out your hand and hail a horse-drawn carriage, just like in the days of yore.
你伸出手就能叫到一辆马车，就像过去的年代一样。

00:33:21.640 --> 00:33:25.020
We like to drive in every weekend from Hasselbrook to take in the sight.
我们喜欢每个周末从哈塞尔布鲁克开车进城来开开眼界。

00:33:25.240 --> 00:33:28.300
I like it for the volatile crowds and the smell of roasting pennies.
我喜欢这里变化无常的人群和烤硬币的气味。

00:33:28.640 --> 00:33:29.840
And I like it for the salt.
而我喜欢这里的盐。

00:33:30.160 --> 00:33:33.640
Salt Alton, those big, splashy shows on the Great White Way.
盐·奥尔顿，百老汇大道上那些大型、华丽的演出。

00:33:33.660 --> 00:33:35.080
We sure do love those shows.
我们确实非常喜欢那些演出。

00:33:35.460 --> 00:33:40.480
I remembered we'd just come from a matinee performance of Palsy, that new musical about the Medicare debates.
我记得我们刚看完音乐剧《小儿麻痹》的日场演出，那是部关于医疗保险辩论的新音乐剧。

00:33:40.940 --> 00:33:41.520
Oh, it was spectacular.
哦，太壮观了。

00:33:42.120 --> 00:33:44.100
The costumes and the dancing.
服装和舞蹈。

00:33:44.220 --> 00:33:46.720
The chorus line on their walkers with the IV stands.
合唱团推着带有静脉注射架的助行器。

00:33:47.100 --> 00:33:48.400
God, I loved that show.
天哪，我太喜欢那个演出了。

00:33:48.620 --> 00:33:57.820
We bought a few dozen scalding pretzels from the passing snack cart, settled into the back seat of our horse-drawn carriage, and had just started rehashing the show when that witch appeared.
我们从路过的零食车上买了几打烫手的蝴蝶结饼，在马车的后座上安顿下来，正开始重新回味那场演出时，那个女巫出现了。

00:33:58.080 --> 00:33:59.340
She wasn't a witch, Linda.
她不是女巫，琳达。

00:33:59.440 --> 00:34:00.540
She was a tattoo artist.
她是个纹身师。

00:34:00.660 --> 00:34:05.140
A tattoo artist with a particularly offensive message etched into her forehead.
一个额头上刻着极其冒犯人字样的纹身师。

00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:14.180
The strange thing, the unusual thing, was that she knocked on the door of our carriage and handed us a simple plastic pail containing a human heart.
奇怪的是，不寻常的是，她敲了敲我们马车的门，递给我们一个装着一颗人类心脏的普通塑料桶。

00:34:14.940 --> 00:34:16.180
Now that was an eye-opener.
这可真是让人大开眼界。

00:34:16.500 --> 00:34:23.840
The girl said that it had been her mother's heart and that she desperately needed to have it delivered to Clydesdale where her brother was awaiting a transplant.
那个女孩说那是她母亲的心脏，她急需把它送到克莱兹代尔，她弟弟正在那里等待移植。

00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:24.100
plant.
移植。

00:34:24.660 --> 00:34:27.980
And Clydesdale, that was out of state, not far from Hasselbrook.
而克莱兹代尔在州外，离哈塞尔布鲁克不远。

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:31.120
She'd intended to deliver it herself, but then something came up.
她原本打算自己送去的，但后来出了点状况。

00:34:31.700 --> 00:34:32.460
A date.
一个约会。

00:34:33.320 --> 00:34:36.580
She'd been invited to a beer blast by a man with a Caesar haircut.
她被一个留着恺撒式发型的男人邀请去参加啤酒派对。

00:34:36.980 --> 00:34:38.140
I like a Caesar.
我挺喜欢恺撒发型的。

00:34:38.460 --> 00:34:40.100
Me, I thought it was some sort of scam.
至于我，我觉得这纯粹是个骗局。

00:34:41.260 --> 00:34:42.820
I've read about things like this in the papers.
我在报纸上读到过类似的事情。

00:34:43.100 --> 00:34:48.620
A couple comes to town to take in a show, and the next thing you know, someone's handing them an organ and picking all the salt off their pretzels.
一对夫妇进城看演出，紧接着你就会发现，有人塞给他们一个器官，还把他们蝴蝶结饼上的盐全抠掉了。

00:34:48.900 --> 00:34:50.860
It's the oldest story in the book.
这是老掉牙的套路了。

00:34:51.060 --> 00:34:56.160
But then she reached into her pocket and pulled out two tickets for Sublet, and what could we say?
但接着她把手伸进口袋，掏出了两张《分租》的门票，我们还能说什么呢？

00:34:56.220 --> 00:34:57.640
That's the hottest show in town.
那是城里最火爆的演出。

00:34:58.040 --> 00:34:59.160
Nobody gets tickets to that.
根本没人能买到票。

00:34:59.560 --> 00:35:03.920
So we said, sure we'll deliver your mother's heart to your sick brother in Clydesdale.
所以我们说，当然可以，我们会把你的母亲的心脏送到克莱兹代尔给你生病的弟弟。

00:35:04.280 --> 00:35:05.980
Because it seemed like the right thing to do.
因为这似乎是正确的事。

00:35:06.180 --> 00:35:08.620
A matinee performance with front row seats.
一场头排座位的日场演出。

00:35:08.660 --> 00:35:08.840
seats.
座位。

00:35:15.800 --> 00:35:17.120
So off we went.
于是我们出发了。

00:35:17.240 --> 00:35:23.580
Our rascal was in the parking lot ten blocks away, but the traffic was an absolute tangle, and it would have taken hours to reach it.
我们的老车就停在十个街区外的停车场，但交通简直乱成一团，走过去得花好几个小时。

00:35:23.800 --> 00:35:29.000
I had the carriage driver take us to the river, where we could have one of those medical waste barges carry us to the other side.
我让车夫带我们去河边，我们可以坐那种医疗废物驳船去对岸。

00:35:30.480 --> 00:35:32.120
The view was remarkable.
景色非凡。

00:35:32.480 --> 00:35:35.500
The sky, the color of a freshly minted nickel.
天空呈现出新铸造的镍币的颜色。

00:35:36.660 --> 00:36:26.740
